  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A quiet developer workbench",
    "overview": "The user approved warm white surfaces, charcoal text and restrained evergreen accents, with code-first implementation. Self-hosted DM Sans supports reading and interface tasks; JetBrains Mono identifies code and measurements. The thesis is to make the transformation from a small JSON template to useful frontend data visible and repeatable.\n\nThis direction was explicitly pinned and confirmed before implementation. The user-pinned-direction exemption applies; this is not a retrospective FORM seed. The concept-seed tool ran (key 45686601); its alternatives do not override the confirmed workbench direction. No approved visual comp exists. This document records the implemented docs/demo artifact rather than inventing visual approval.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper, charcoal reading text and evergreen interaction states.",
      "Fine separators and flat, readable work areas.",
      "Visible schema/result relationships and explicit data provenance.",
      "Reading-first guides and task-focused demos."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Restrained Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use evergreen for actions, links and active state; let neutral surfaces carry the page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Code Rule",
        "body": "Nested code inherits its preformatted panel's size. Code panels use the code role; mobile guide and homepage examples use 12px. Do not compound the global inline-code scaling inside a preformatted block.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Separator Rule",
        "body": "Establish panel boundaries with fine lines and surface tone.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** pair schemas with their results and keep sample/live provenance explicit.",
      "**Do** use the recorded font roles and preserve readable code sizing.",
      "**Do** retain labeled fields, visible keyboard focus, data alternatives and mobile disclosures.",
      "**Do** use borders and restrained surface changes to organize work."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce gradients, glass or ornamental shadows into the approved workbench.",
      "**Don't** invent customer proof, performance claims or production-traffic metrics.",
